cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research or solid dispersion formulation studies, please cite it as below."
title: "PharmaPolySCOPE Physicochemical Input Generator: Authoritative Upstream Parameter Engine for Solid Dispersion Formulation Modeling"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pharmapolyscope/pharmapolyscope-input-generator"
keywords:
  - "pharmaceutical-engineering"
  - "amorphous-solid-dispersions"
  - "solubility-parameters"
  - "hansen-solubility-parameters"
  - "rdkit"
  - "cheminformatics"
  - "quality-by-design"
  - "uncertainty-quantification"
  - "monte-carlo"
  - "formulation-screening"
abstract: >-
  The PharmaPolySCOPE Upstream Physicochemical Input Generator is an authoritative,
  open-source scientific application and decision-support engine for amorphous solid
  dispersion (ASD) formulation workflows. It resolves the severe upstream data quality
  crisis in pharmaceutical literature by standardizing neutral molecular structures,
  evaluating Boyer–Kauzmann glass transition heuristics (Tg = 0.70 × Tm), decomposing
  substructures via Fedors group increments, computing 3D Hoftyzer–van Krevelen Hansen
  Solubility Parameters, and conducting 10,000-trial Monte Carlo uncertainty quantification
  (95% Bayesian CIs). The software enforces a rigorous 12-gate quality control battery
  and exports standardized, zero-spill single-page PDF certificates (PharmaPolySCOPE Ready
  Sheets) compliant with ICH Q8/Q9 Quality-by-Design guidelines.
authors:
  - family-names: "Formulation Science & Computational Chemistry Team"
    given-names: "PharmaPolySCOPE Research Consortium"
    affiliation: "Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences & Advanced Drug Delivery"
